\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $d\geq 3$ and $\beta \geq 0$, is the free zero-field Ising measure on the d-regular tree a factor of iid exactly when $tanh(\beta )\leq (d-1)^{-1/2}$, including equality? In that range ask for a Borel factor commuting with every graph automorphism on every label input.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $d\geq 3$ and $\beta \geq 0$, is the free zero-field Ising measure on the d-regular tree a factor of iid exactly when $tanh(\beta )\leq (d-1)^{-1/2}$, including equality? In that range ask for a Borel factor commuting with every graph automorphism on every label input.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-sharp-factor-of-IID-threshold-for-the-free-Ising-model-on-regular-trees-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex}.
